\description{
Imports another tool's segmentation into a dataset, in the Segmentation view, which shows it: a SpatialData Zarr store (spatialdata), Baysor's segmentation.csv with its polygons (baysor), GeoJSON polygons with an optional transcript table (geojson), a Xenium Ranger output bundle of the same run (xenium), or a folder of SituCraft's own segmentation files, as `situcraft refine` writes them (situcraft). A job reads it, checks it against the dataset (the transcripts it names, where its cells lie, its ids) and records it as a segmentation artifact with the files' SHA-256; an import whose check finds a fatal problem is recorded as invalid. Coordinates are read in units (um, else pixels of the morphology image), never guessed. Needs the token (it reads files).
}
